# Content roots to migrate from AEM → Sanity.
#
# This file defines the AEM pages the content CLI walks. For each page, the
# resulting Sanity doc is populated with `slug: { _type: "slug", current: "..." }`
# so the URL lines up with AEM.
#
# Syntax:
#   # ...                    → comment (also allowed inline after content)
#   @base /content/...       → sets the base path for subsequent relative entries
#   home                     → relative slug, joined as `<base>/home`
#   plans/consumer/phones/x  → relative nested path, joined as `<base>/plans/consumer/phones/x`
#   /content/other/top       → absolute JCR path (slug = "top", the last segment)
#
# Relative entries may include `/` — they're joined onto `@base` verbatim. The
# Sanity doc's `slug.current` defaults to the last segment of the resolved JCR
# path, matching AEM's own page-slug semantics. So with `@base /content/uxp/us/en`,
#   `plans/consumer/phones/experience-beyond-plan`
# resolves to `/content/uxp/us/en/plans/consumer/phones/experience-beyond-plan`
# with `slug: experience-beyond-plan`.
#
# Set MIGRATION_SLUG_STRATEGY=path (see .env.example) to instead use the
# base-relative path exactly as authored here as the slug:
#   `slug: plans/consumer/phones/experience-beyond-plan`.
#
# Multiple @base sections are allowed — each @base applies until the next one.
#
# Tip for discovering paths: hit `<AEM_AUTHOR_URL>/content.1.json` while
# logged into AEM author to list top-level site roots. Drill down one level at
# a time (`/content/<sitename>.1.json`, etc.) until you reach your locale.

@base /content/<your-site>/<locale>

home
about
products
support
support/troubleshooting/devices/phones        # nested paths share the @base
